= Support limits and algebraic boundaries <support-limits>

A verified generic-open decomposition is a geometry certificate, not a complete
integration artifact. The source density must also admit consistent causal
continuation, endpoint treatment and complete chart coverage. The supported
scalar results meet their respective admission conditions; they do not establish
a general resolver for arbitrary algebraic boundaries. The two difficult cases
below make that distinction concrete.

The campaign stops at preparation for the no-contour double box. Neither the
scalar nor the physical-numerator double box has a complete
no-contour artifact or integral estimate. The massive kite also lacks a complete
no-contour integral. Their successful contour comparisons remain in the opening
tables. The measurements here describe *preparation diagnostics* and are not
substitutes for missing generation, integration or convergence measurements.

== Double box: complete geometry, incomplete density resolution

At the exact rational physical point, symGCAD solves and independently verifies
*644,699 original generic-open cells* over the full positive projective domain,
retaining both signs of $F$. The scalar and physical-numerator sources share
this denominator geometry. Positive homogeneous reduction at $x_0$, conditional
quadratic elimination in $x_2$, and lifting order
$[x_0,x_1,x_3,x_4,x_5,x_6,x_2]$ produce the admitted decomposition. The internal
monotone base has 464,265 cells; it is not a smaller complete original atlas.

