== What the local certificates establish

Native general improvements cover source-owned constant endpoints through
degree 32, exact coefficient extraction for tight dyadic brackets, recursive
fan replacements, original-certificate replay under positive rational scaling,
and canonicalization of composed measures. Symbolica supplies the algebra;
symGCAD retains selected-root and domain authority. Original denominators,
ancestry, causal phases and each Jacobian remain explicit. These capabilities
do not constitute an automatic resolution of every moving algebraic boundary.

For original double-box cell 0, the complete *156-term physical open density*
was composed without expanding its algebraic roots inside the numerator.
Four infinity charts passed 6,864 term comparisons, 44 summed-density checks
and 154 independent coordinate/Jacobian checks at 128/256 bits. The density
checks retain an independently evaluated lower-lip phase; directed-ball checks
certify the tested coordinates and Jacobians. Exact finite-depth series also
found a common $c^3$ infinity power in all 624 term/chart combinations, with
epsilon cancelling. Those local coefficients are not truncated bulk integrands
or certificates for the remaining direction faces and causal seams.

A separate scalar admission diagnostic completed *307 closed charts of one
original cell*, retaining the full regulator density on the common sufficient
strip $-3/2<Re(epsilon)<1$. It took 4,122.9 seconds and peaked at 9.96 GB aggregate
RSS in a debug preparation driver. It produced *zero compiled kernels and zero
integral estimates*. It does not admit the physical numerator. Its source-bound
objects ended with the process; saved receipts alone do not reconstruct their
source authority.

Catalogue sharing reduces 3,868,194 per-cell axis occurrences to 1,556,848
prefix nodes, a factor of 2.485; repeated root-bound uses reduce by 3.003.
The 260 distinct global boundary polynomials and 45 global support classes do
not prove equality of branches, maps, densities or closed domains. Compatibility
merging retains original cells and excluded seams; no measured merged endpoint
atlas is available.

For scale only, one chart per original cell would give 644,699 charts; 307 per
cell would give 197,922,593. These are *illustrations, neither predictions nor
bounds*. One admitted cell does not support a whole-atlas sector-count,
runtime, memory or artifact-size forecast. The unresolved closed-family
continuation/compiler bridge remains separate from the successful geometry.

== Massive kite: a boundary is not a complete interval

The equal-five-mass kite at $p^2=16$ has *9,840 verified original cells*.
A selected fourth boundary closes over three integration directions in all
*ten replacement charts of cell 0*, passing *40 strict checks at 128/256 bits*.
That result does not close the fourth interval. Its width, denominators and
root-gap intersection with the upper face must join the full original $U$,
$F$, numerator and Jacobian inventory. In particular,
$F^(-1-2epsilon)$ requires common-strip continuation and symbolic subtraction.

A native divided-difference probe verifies candidate width and root identities,
including higher-degree controls. Positivity on every closed face, complete
interval densities, automatic coverage of the other 9,839 cells and full
Laurent compilation remain unfinished. This is a substantive implementation
gap, not evidence that the integral is physically inadmissible or that GCAD
failed. A future general resolver must cover these obligations before claiming
whole-integral support.

The immutable recipes, measurements and source/reuse audits are indexed in
`docs/reviews/no-contour-final-scope.md`,
`docs/no-contour-gghh-verified.json` and the
`examples/no_deformation/gghh_feasibility/` inputs. Historical failed trials and
local diagnostics remain available there; they are not benchmark rows.
